## 📁 Project Architecture
smart-bin-system/
├── backend/
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── User.js          # User & Admin schema with bcrypt hooks
│   │   └── Bin.js           # Bin telemetry, officer & gamification schema
│   ├── iotSimulator.js      # Background IoT telemetry & alert simulator
│   ├── server.js            # Express REST API server & auth routes
│   └── .env                 # Database URI & configuration secrets
└── frontend/
└── src/
└── app/
├── page.js          # Main Sign In / Registration Page
├── dashboard/
│   └── page.js      # Admin Monitoring Dashboard & Leaderboard
└── officer/
└── page.js      # Field Officer Task Portal

---

## 🔒 Backend Authentication & Cloud Highlights

### 1. **MongoDB Atlas Cloud Persistence**
Hosted on MongoDB Atlas cloud clusters for continuous availability, handling user accounts, real-time device telemetry, and officer score tracking.

### 2. **Secure Passwords & JWT Tokens**
- Passwords are salted and hashed using `bcryptjs` in a pre-save Mongoose hook before storing.
- Generates signed JWTs for session authorization across protected API routes.

### 3. **Role & Security Code Verification**
- **Admin Operators**: Access central monitoring dashboards via verified credentials.
- **Field Officers**: Quick authentication using pre-assigned numeric security pins (`1001`–`1004`).

---

## 🚀 Environment Setup & Installation

### Prerequisites
- **Node.js**: v18.x or higher
- **MongoDB Atlas Connection String**: (`MONGO_URI`)

### Step 1: Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/Abhiranjan-123/Smart-Bin-Management-System.git](https://github.com/Abhiranjan-123/Smart-Bin-Management-System.git)
cd Smart-Bin-Management-System
Step 2: Configure Environment Variables (backend/.env)Create a .env file inside the backend folder:Code snippetPORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.mongodb.net/smartbin?retryWrites=true&w=majority
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key
Step 3: Install DependenciesBash# Install backend dependencies
cd backend
npm install

# Install frontend dependencies
cd ../frontend
npm install
⚙️ Running the ApplicationOpen 3 separate terminal windows inside VS Code:Terminal 1: Backend API ServerBashcd backend
npm start
Runs on http://localhost:5000Terminal 2: IoT Telemetry SimulatorBashcd backend
npm run simulator
Simulates real-time bin capacity increases and triggers critical alerts in MongoDB Atlas.Terminal 3: Next.js FrontendBashcd frontend
npm run dev
